<in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnFinancialResultsExplanatoryTextBlock contextRef="OneD">1.The above Consolidated Financial Results of Ramco Systems Limited India the Company its subsidiaries together referred to as Group and its Associate were reviewed by the Audit Committee and approved by the Board in its meeting held on 07th February 2024. The Results are prepared in accordance with the Ind AS as prescribed under Section 133 of the Companies Act read with the relevant rules issued thereunder. The Statutory Auditors have carried out a limited review of the Results of the Group for the nine months ended 31st Dec 2023 and have issued an unmodified audit report. 2.Employee benefits expense includes cost reversal of cost towards the proportionate fair value of the stock options granted to various employees, amortised over the graded vesting period. Refer UAFR PDF filed for break up. 3.Other expenses includes bad debts provision for doubtful debts and advances. Refer UAFR PDF filed for break up. 4.Other expenses also includes foreign exchange fluctuation loss gain. Refer UAFR PDF filed for break up. 5.Other expenses also includes provision for customer obligations. Refer UAFR PDF filed for breakup.6. During the quarter the Company had allotted 51174 equity shares under the ESOPs. Accordingly the paid up capital of the Company increased to Rs.353.91 Mln. USD 6.63 Mln. as at 31st December 2023 from Rs.353.39 Mln. USD 6.63 Mln. as at 30th September 2023. 7.The utilisation of the proceeds of Preferential Issue 2022. Refer UAFR PDF filed for break up. Balance available as on 31st Dec 2023 is Nil. 8.Status of Borrowing. Refer UAFR PDF filed for break up. 9.The Group has only one operating segment Software Solutions and Services. 10. Figures for the previous periods have been regrouped restated wherever necessary to make them comparable with the figures for the current  periods.</in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnFinancialResultsExplanatoryTextBlock>
